B.WU=s(['Mentioned as "Prabhu Mountains" in the Kalika Purana and Mahabharata.',"Associated with sage Parashuram (atoned for sin at Parshuram Kund), Sage Vyasa, King Bhismaka, and Lord Krishna marrying Rukmini.","Pre-1954: Known as North-East Frontier Tracts (NEFT) under the Ministry of External Affairs, advised by Lt. N.K. Rustomji ICS.","1954: North East Frontier Regulation (Administration) Act of 1954 renamed the area to North-East Frontier Agency (NEFA).","1969: Agency Council constituted as the apex advisory body (20 members, first sitting 3rd Dec 1969 inaugurated by Assam Governor B.K. Nehru).",'10-11 August 1970: In its 2nd session at Shillong, the Council chose the name "Arunachal Pradesh" over Udayachal and Brahma Mandal.',"1971: North Eastern Areas (Reorganisation) Act, 1971 separated NEFA from Assam and created the Union Territory of Arunachal Pradesh on 20th January 1972 under Chief Commissioner K.A.A. Raja.","1st June 1974: State capital shifted from Shillong to Itanagar (inaugurated by President V.V. Giri).","15th August 1975: Pradesh Council converted into a Provisional Legislative Assembly; Prem Khandu Thungon sworn in as 1st Chief Minister.","February 1978: First general election to the Legislative Assembly was held.","20th February 1987: Conferred full statehood as 24th State of India under 55th Amendment Act, 1986."],t.s)
B.hb={Event:0,Year:1}
